and protect hearing."},{"id":"3.1","title":"Musical Sounds","strand":3,"lessons":14,"outcomes":["Identify sound sources involving people, animals, birds and ordinary objects.","Distinguish loud/soft, fast/slow and high/low qualities in sounds.","Express personal responses to environmental sounds.","Describe the mood evoked by a short musical passage.","Enjoy listening carefully and talking about music."],"experiences":["Listen to and identify sounds from familiar environments.","Compare paired examples for volume, speed and pitch.","Respond to short music or sounds with appropriate words, drawings or movement and describe the mood."],"inquiry":["How do we identify sound qualities and what they make us feel?"],"resources":"Voices, nearby sounds, picture cards and optional short sound recordings.","assessment":"Check sound-source recognition, comparison of qualities, mood responses and respectful listening.","competencies":"Communication; creative imagination; cultural sensitivity.","safety":"Avoid excessive sound levels; offer visual or vibration cues for varied hearing needs."},{"id":"3.2","title":"Water Safety Awareness","strand":3,"lessons":14,"outcomes":["Identify common water collection and storage points near home.","Recognise dangers associated with household and community water locations.","Make a picture montage showing water points.","Describe safe behaviour near different water sources.","Value water safety as an everyday life-protection habit."],"experiences":["Examine pictures of tanks, containers, wells, rivers and other local water points.","Discuss realistic dangers and identify safer behaviour and when to seek adult help.","Create a picture montage showing water sources, warning signs and safety actions."],"inquiry":["How can we recognise and avoid danger around water?"],"resources":"Pictures of water points, paper, glue, warning-sign images and adult-approved rules.","assessment":"Check recognition of water points and hazards, montage accuracy, safe-action descriptions and responsible behaviour.","competencies":"Communication; personal responsibility; health and safety awareness.","safety":"Use classroom pictures and discussions; never take young learners to unsafe water sites for this activity."}]$vs_g1$::jsonb as units),
